blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:670:	None of the following is a named statement of the source article; each isolates one step of the Lean proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:ms-rigidity}. Let $(X_{\mathrm A}, Z_{\mathrm A})$ and $(X_{\mathrm B}, Z_{\mathrm B})$ be pairs of $\pm 1$-valued observables on the two players' spaces, let $A_b = X_{\mathrm A}^b P^{Z_{\mathrm A}}_b$ and $B_c = X_{\mathrm B}^c P^{Z_{\mathrm B}}_c$ be the residual factors of the two controlled swaps, and let $v$ be any vector on the bipartite space. If $b \ne c$ then $\|(A_b \ot B_c) v\|$ is at most half of $\|(Z_{\mathrm A} \ot I - I \ot Z_{\mathrm B}) v\|$, and the two diagonal components $(A_0 \ot B_0)v$ and $(A_1 \ot B_1)v$ differ by at most the sum of the two cross-player distances of the pair on $v$ and half the norm of $(X_{\mathrm A} Z_{\mathrm A} + Z_{\mathrm A} X_{\mathrm A}) \ot I$ on $v$. Neither estimate uses Bob's anticommutator, and neither assumes $v$ normalized.
